backport: bound xps metadata and epub outline recursion (bug 709480)

BACKPORT of upstream mupdf b8aa2f4254e5c040ac683553055c6e371de4e706, not a
change of ours. Drop it when the vendored mupdf moves past that commit - it is
on mupdf master but not in 1.28.2.

https://bugs.ghostscript.com/show_bug.cgi?id=709480

Deeply nested metadata recurses until the stack overflows. Bounds the depth at
100 in xps_parse_metadata_imp(), and in the two epub outline parsers
(epub_parse_ncx_imp, epub_parse_nav_imp) that have the same weakness.

This replaces our own 0017-xps-bound-metadata-recursion, which fixed the XPS
half of it for issue #5032 with the same mechanism and a limit of 256. Upstream
guards the two epub paths as well, so taking theirs is strictly more coverage
and one less patch of ours to re-merge. Verified on the #5032 repro: it opens
with the same diagnostics and no stack overflow either way.
---
diff --git a/source/html/epub-doc.c b/source/html/epub-doc.c
index 67cea90..4bf1144 100644
--- a/source/html/epub-doc.c
+++ b/source/html/epub-doc.c
